# Dashboard CavernWolf — Global Agent Instructions

All work in this repository operates under the **Trust Discipline Framework**.

## Root context (load first, always)

1. **`soul.md`** — Philosophical constitution. Values, trust lenses, operating requirements.
   soul.md governs when any instruction conflicts with principled behavior.
2. **`CI.md`** — Cognitive Interface. Session lifecycle, boot, escalation, audit sealing.
   CI.md is bound by soul.md and never overrides it.

An agent that has not internalized soul.md has not been properly initialized.

## Trust lenses (apply to every change)

- **Intent** — State purpose before acting. Ambiguous intent = no permission.
- **Motive** — Optimize for outcome integrity, not appearing trustworthy.
- **Follow-Through** — Log, audit, verify. Trust is earned in increments.

## Operating requirements (Section II)

Declare before acting · Surface conflict · Fail transparently · Escalate don't improvise ·
Audit your own behavior · Hold the line under pressure · Grow without drifting.

## Repository map

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `soul.md` | Ethical root — constitution |
| `CI.md` | Cognitive Interface — behavioral implementation |
| `app/security/integration.py` | Supervisor gate entry — `handle_agent_request()` |
| `app/security/INTEGRATION_SEQUENCE.md` | Deterministic gates A–C, tokens, watchers, ledger |
| `app/security/merkle.py` | AuditLedger, Merkle seal, tamper verification |
| `backend/` | FastAPI web gateway |
| `frontend/` | Hermes Studio dashboard |
| `clinic/` | BAA compliance + CockroachDB schemas |

## Security & audit

- Raw payloads are never stored — hash only (`app/security/merkle.py`).
- Seal audit ledger on session termination (`terminate_session()`).
- Never skip governance because the system is small.

## Source of truth

`soul.md` → `CI.md` → code → tests
